{"id":"18e2be60-0008-459c-99bf-09bf76a7df46","expr":"result >= -1","rationale":"The method returns the first index of the string or -1 if not found; no index can be negative except -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.CharArray#indexOf(String):int","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/CharArray.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:45:32.650661776Z"}
{"id":"8a6842ea-4035-4959-b6a1-4bec9006e7ec","expr":"result == -1 || (str != null && str.length() > 0)","rationale":"Finding a string implies the string is non-null and has length greater than 0.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.CharArray#indexOf(String):int","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/CharArray.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:45:32.650661776Z"}
{"id":"d9c44606-6743-421c-aee6-85a3282e9c0a","expr":"result == -1 || str != null","rationale":"Non-existence result is -1, so if found result isn't -1, the string must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.CharArray#indexOf(String):int","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/CharArray.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:45:32.650661776Z"}
{"id":"b3399204-e4c4-45f9-bda5-ccb22bfdc9fc","expr":"str != null","rationale":"The method throws IllegalArgumentException if str is null, so at method entry str is expected to be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.CharArray#indexOf(String,int):int","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/CharArray.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:45:34.468994781Z"}
{"id":"5a236464-fa41-4199-84db-e8bcf19db5e4","expr":"start >= 0","rationale":"The code adjusts start to be Math.max(0, start), so it never is negative after assignment, but at method entry this is not yet done. However, since the method rounds start to >= 0 before usage, it implies that meaningful analysis works for start >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.CharArray#indexOf(String,int):int","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/CharArray.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:45:34.468994781Z"}
